    "notes": [
      {
        "category": "summary",
        "text": "Security update for python-Brotli",
        "title": "Title of the patch"
      },
      {
        "category": "description",
        "text": "This update for python-Brotli fixes the following issues:\n\n- CVE-2025-6176: denial of service (DoS) due to a flaw in its brotli decompression (bsc#1252945).\n- CVE-2026-111497: Brotli decoder out-of-bounds write permits remote code execution (bsc#1287779).\n\nUpdate to 1.2.1:\n\n- **decoder / encoder: added static initialization to reduce binary size**\n- python: allow limiting decoder output (see SECURITY section)\n- python: modernize extension / allow multi-phase module initialization\n- decoder / encoder: static tables use \"small\" model (allows 2GiB+ binaries)\n",
        "title": "Description of the patch"
      },
      {
        "category": "details",
        "text": "openSUSE-Leap-16.0-2002",
        "title": "Patchnames"
      },
